# 0006: a decision KV region, and two tap read-path fixes
#
# Apply from the tree root:  patch -p1 < 0006-decision-region-and-tap-read-path.patch
# (paths are a/... b/... against a Strata 0.1.41 source tree)
#
# 1. The decision region.  --decision-cache-mib / --decision-cache-slots add a SECOND parked-conversation
#    cache.  A request that passes `cache_region=decision` parks into and restores from that instance alone.
#    The live session remembers the region it came from, so a conversation the decode side produced is always
#    parked back into the normal region - an extraction arriving in the middle of a chat cannot push that
#    chat's snapshot into the region the extractions evict.  The decision region's parked conversations are
#    deliberately not counted by --kv-grow, so a throwaway prompt never holds VRAM the decode side could use.
#    Acceptance (tmp_scripts/strata_ro/cache_iso_test.py): 20 decision requests overran the region and evicted
#    it 19 times while the normal region's eviction counter stayed 0, and the normal conversation was still
#    restorable afterwards (867 tokens restored).
#
# 2. windows_ok(): a tap request (latt / latspans) takes the hooked verify-window path.  The batched read_part
#    path and the pipelined loop have no tap hooks, so a prompt that did not happen to fit one short segment
#    (--short-read, 64 by default) came back with NO rows at all: a 95-token prompt returned 0 segments while
#    a 59-token one returned all of them.
#
# 3. A tap request always reads from token 0.  Tap rows exist only for the tokens this request itself pushed
#    through the windows, so a prefix restored from the parked cache, continued from the live session or copied
#    from a batch slot returns no rows for the spans it covered (measured: asking the same prompt twice returned
